'''''Pterolepis''''' is a [[genus]] of flowering plant in the family [[Melastomataceae]].<ref>{{PLANTS|id=PTERO5|taxon=Pterolepis|accessdate=29 July 2018}}</ref> Within Melastomataceae, it forms a [[clade]] with genus ''[[Pterogastra]]''.<ref name=":0">{{Cite journal|last=Kriebel|first=Ricardo|last2=Almeda|first2=Frank|last3=Penneys|first3=Darin S.|last4=Guimaraes|first4=Paulo J. F.|last5=Michelangeli|first5=Fabián A.|date=2013-01-01|title=Phylogenetic relationships and distribution of New World Melastomeae (Melastomataceae)|journal=Botanical Journal of the Linnean Society|language=en|volume=171|issue=1|pages=38–60|doi=10.1111/j.1095-8339.2012.01295.x|issn=0024-4074|doi-access=free}}</ref>  
''Pterolepis'' contains some fifteen species, all of which are found in the [[Neotropical realm|Neotropical geographic realmm]].<ref name=":0" /> Most species are concentrated in [[Brazil]], with a few others across [[Central America|Central]] and [[South America]].<ref name=":0" /><ref>{{Cite journal|last=Renner|first=Susanne S.|date=1994|title=A revision of Pterolepis (Melastomataceae: Melastomeae)|journal=Nordic Journal of Botany|language=en|volume=14|issue=1|pages=73–104|doi=10.1111/j.1756-1051.1994.tb00575.x|issn=1756-1051}}</ref>

